   "html_text": "Testimonia indicate that Anaxagoras thinks the Earth is flat and drum-like in shape (DK 59A87). In connection with this thesis, Panchenko 1997 contends that Anaxagoras advances an argument against the sphericity of the Earth. Anaxagoras’ commitment to the solidity of the Earth, Moon, and Sun, and both his theory of eclipses and his theory of comets, are outlined above, in section 1. We are told that Anaxagoras thinks the Milky Way is reflected starlight, that shooting stars are sparks generated ",
